# Visual Consistency

If Figma exists:

Reproduce it faithfully.

If it does not:

The CRM V4 Design System becomes the visual source of truth.

The new component must match the existing:

- Buttons
- Inputs
- Cards
- Tables
- Calendar
- Charts
- Dialogs
- Forms
- Navigation
- Feedback
- Typography

Never create a component that looks visually disconnected from the Design System.

---

# Autonomous Design Rule

Do not ask for Figma or screenshots for every component.

Assume that many Design System foundation components will not have dedicated designs.

When no reference exists:

Continue using the CRM V4 Design System.

Only request additional design references when reproducing a very specific interface is impossible without them.

---

# Output

Deliver:

- Production-ready component
- Complete component family (when applicable)
- CRM V4 Design System compliant
- Styleguide documentation
- Responsive
- Accessible
- Dark Mode compatible
- Semantic Design Tokens
- Real examples
- Reusable architecture

---

# Principles

✔ Figma overrides everything when provided.

✔ Screenshots override the Design System when provided.

✔ The Design System is the default visual source when no references exist.

✔ The Markdown documentation defines behavior and business rules.

✔ shadcn/ui is infrastructure only.

✔ Every component must strengthen the CRM V4 Design System.

✔ Build systems, not isolated components.